# Synthetic consumer fixture for isolated qualification (scripts/qualify_packs.py
# unions each pack against only its own ontology.ttl plus this opt-in fixture,
# never a sibling pack's real ontology.ttl).
#
# stl:sregym-run-kubectl-claim (ontology.ttl) deliberately references a REAL,
# already-admitted fact -- dcp:sregym-run-kubectl -- which is typed for real at
# packs/domain-capability-pack/ontology.ttl (dcp:sregym-run-kubectl a
# dcp:Capability). That fact is real and correct; it is simply not visible to
# THIS pack's isolated qualification graph unless restated here as a synthetic
# stub, which is exactly the mechanism scripts/qualify_packs.py's own docstring
# names for this situation ("qualification/consumer.ttl ... add synthetic
# consumer facts to projection/semantic qualification graphs").
#
# This stub intentionally carries ONLY the one triple gates/010_no_skipped_states.rq's
# second UNION branch needs (`?fact a ?anyType`) -- it is not a full copy of
# domain-capability-pack's ontology, and it does not assert anything beyond
# "this IRI is a typed individual," so it cannot mask a real defect in
# domain-capability-pack itself (a full duplicate would risk drifting from the
# real source; this minimal stub cannot).
#
# (Merged with a duplicate "Standalone marketplace qualification fixture" stub
# introduced independently on origin/main -- both stubs asserted the exact
# same single triple below; this comment keeps the more detailed rationale.)
@prefix dcp: <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/domain-capability#> .

dcp:sregym-run-kubectl a dcp:Capability .
